  "title": "Human-AI collaboration for co-managing epilepsy in real time: scalp EEG and SEEG from 13 epilepsy monitoring unit patients",
  "description": "Continuous video-EEG recordings from 13 patients with epilepsy at the Penn Level 4 Epilepsy Monitoring Unit, comprising scalp EEG (11 patients) and stereo-EEG (2 patients) across 69 recording days. The data support an inpatient prototype in which a conversational AI agent on the patient's smartphone is linked to the EEG, and seizure detection is retrained using patient and clinician feedback. Annotations include seizures, patient push-button events, sleep stages, medications and patient reports made through the human-AI platform. Model outputs are provided as derivatives.",
  "methods_description": "Continuous scalp EEG (256 Hz, 46 channels) and SEEG (1024 Hz depth contacts) were recorded as one EDF per recording day during clinical monitoring. Annotation CSVs were converted to BIDS events.tsv. Processing for the seizure detection models used a 0.5-100 Hz bandpass for scalp and 0.5-250 Hz for intracranial EEG, 60 and 120 Hz notch filters, and common average or bipolar re-referencing. Dates in the EDF headers were shifted to protect privacy.",
